0045:     """
0046:     Replace every repeated placeholder object with the matching colored sprite and erase the original sprite.
0047: 
0048:     Input structure:
0049:     - The dominant background surrounds one connected polychromatic source sprite.
0050:     - A separate monochrome placeholder color forms multiple 4-connected target objects.
0051:     - Each target object has the same normalized mask as the source sprite.
0052: 
0053:     Rule:
0054:     - Infer the placeholder color as the unique foreground color whose components
0055:       match the mask of the remaining connected source sprite.
0056:     - Clear the original source sprite to background.
0057:     - Paint the source sprite's colors onto each matching placeholder object at
0058:       the target object's bbox position.
0059: 
0060:     Key insight:
0061:     The placeholder objects are unlabeled copies of the source mask; their pixels inherit colors from the corresponding cells of the source sprite.
0062:     """
